1
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:02,800
Everyone in Bangkok knows Thatri.

2
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:05,800
Too bad his stupid decisions
left him completely broke.

3
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,919
Why the sudden trip to Bangkok?

4
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,639
I'm going to dig into Thatri's past.

5
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:13,640
<i>Maybe I can get rid of him</i>
<i>without wasting a single bullet.</i>

6
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,320
What is the meaning of this?

7
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,240
This is him.

8
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,840
He's pretending to be Mr. Thatri
for the inheritance.

9
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:23,720
He's just trying to steal it.
Take him to the police station.

10
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,040
<i>Who do you suspect?</i>

11
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:27,800
I need a bit more evidence.

12
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:31,560
I still don't understand
why he did all of this.

13
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,760
Hey,

14
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:43,680
why did you let Vijarn take over?

15
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:45,400
Isn't this going a bit too far?

16
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,920
Aunt Paetai,

17
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,120
I can't handle this all by myself.

18
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:52,440
Besides, your hands are completely full.

19
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:56,440
Right now, he's the most
trustworthy person we have.

20
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:59,960
If he doesn't help, who will?

21
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:03,040
This is too much.

22
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:04,960
Vijarn is just an employee.

23
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:07,480
He isn't even good enough to court you,

24
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:10,160
yet you're allowing him
to meddle in our business?

25
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:15,640
If things between
Mr. Vijarn and me go any further,

26
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:19,960
he'll eventually have to help
manage our business.

27
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:23,320
Hey. Are you actually accepting his love?

28
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:27,640
We haven't agreed
to anything that serious yet.

29
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:32,360
But as a woman
handling so many businesses alone,

30
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:38,120
shouldn't I at least
have a man by my side to help?

31
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:02,560
Thank you for picking
a rental room in this area.

32
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:06,160
With so many people around,
nobody would dare to mess with me.

33
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:09,520
We didn't choose this place
for your safety, Uncle Ree.

34
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:16,320
We picked it solely because it's cheap.
You're tight on cash, after all.

35
00:04:16,399 --> 00:04:19,600
If we picked an expensive one,
you wouldn't be able to afford it.

36
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,360
What a pity.

37
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:29,200
You're incredibly handsome,
but poverty ruins everything.

38
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:31,000
Good looks won't put food on the table.

39
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:35,000
That's brutally honest.

40
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,760
The room is just over there.

41
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,200
Let's go.

42
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,560
A foolish woman like Rajit

43
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:52,240
can't achieve anything without my help.

44
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,320
She won't escape my grasp.

45
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:57,080
But her relatives probably
won't back down so easily.

46
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,640
I'll handle them myself.

47
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:02,720
What are the updates on Thatri?

48
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,360
I have men tailing him.

49
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:08,040
He's renting a room in the market,
but the place is always crowded.

50
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:10,440
It won't be easy to ambush and kill him.

51
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:14,080
If killing him is that difficult,

52
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,440
then flush him out instead.

53
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:19,400
Right?

54
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,960
Ever set a fire
to drive animals out of hiding?

55
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:42,920
Barking at this hour?

56
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,960
I should send Don Jose
to teach you a lesson.

57
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:02,200
Who's burning something at this hour?

58
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:07,880
Hey!

59
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:11,760
Today I'm just having some fun with you.

60
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:14,240
I'll finish the job next time.

61
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,800
Somebody help! Fire!

62
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:25,080
Help! Fire!

63
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:27,760
-Fire!
-Please help me put it out!

64
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:28,840
Help.

65
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:30,760
-Fire!
-Fire!

66
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:34,560
Hurry.

67
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,640
-Hurry!
-Fire!

68
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:40,160
Hurry up!

69
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:42,160
Hurry up!

70
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,880
Put out the fire.

71
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,280
-Who the hell set this fire?
-Right?

72
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,400
-Don't know.
-No idea.

73
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,440
I didn't see anyone

74
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:58,440
THALANG PROVINCIAL POLICE STATION

75
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,720
That's all there is to it.

76
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:03,240
Thank you for coming in
to give your statement.

77
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,440
Of course.

78
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,880
Have some coffee. It'll help wake you up.

79
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:19,000
Thank you.

80
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:29,240
I must be destined for the station.

81
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,360
I haven't even been out for a day,
and here I am again.

82
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:35,640
It's good enough that you're safe.

83
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:41,800
They forced me out of that place
so I'd have nowhere else to go.

84
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,040
So what?

85
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:47,760
You can just move somewhere else.
There's nothing to fear.

86
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:51,520
Who would let me rent?
I'd only bring them bad luck.

87
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:53,360
I would.

88
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:57,840
I'm not afraid of bad luck.

89
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:01,440
Just move into my house.
You won't even have to pay rent.

90
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:04,000
I couldn't do that, District Chief.
I'd feel bad.

91
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,800
Besides, you're not living alone anymore.

92
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:11,800
Having me there would just
make things awkward. I can't go.

93
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:29,680
Sorry to bother you.

94
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:33,520
It's fine. You're going
through a tough time.

95
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:36,559
Hardship after hardship,

96
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:40,760
now you're homeless.
A little help isn't too much to ask.

97
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,240
I'm deeply grateful.

98
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:46,320
So, how many days will you be staying?

99
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:49,720
If it's just a day or two,
I can prepare some extra food for you.

100
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:55,160
Well, until his case is fully resolved.

101
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,680
So, it'll probably take five or six years.

102
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:01,320
You're incredibly lucky, Tri,

103
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:03,680
to have such a good friend
like my son-in-law.

104
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:11,120
It's probably the reward
for my mother's good deeds.

105
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:14,000
Back then, whenever
you were short on cash,

106
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:16,360
she'd always lend you money

107
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:17,920
without charging an interest.

108
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,120
This blessing is finally helping me out.

109
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:21,800
Tri…

110
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:27,480
I've already prepared a room for you.
Go take a look upstairs.

111
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:30,080
Please tell me if you need anything.

112
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:35,000
Thank you. Please excuse me then.

113
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:40,800
Right this way, Mr. Thatri.

114
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:12,360
You're not here
to complain about Tri, are you?

115
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:14,080
Don't read my mind.

116
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:16,040
I'll tell you straight.

117
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:18,000
I don't want Tri staying here.

118
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:21,200
That's impossible, Mother.

119
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:22,720
And why on earth not?

120
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:26,400
Tri and I grew up together.

121
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:30,160
He's in deep trouble.
How can we be so heartless?

122
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:34,120
Besides, Bundit was the one
who invited him to stay.

123
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,600
Then tell him to throw him out.

124
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:38,280
I heard

125
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:41,120
Tri has been causing trouble
all over Phuket.

126
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:43,040
Do you want to get dragged into this?

127
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:47,680
If Bundit isn't afraid, then neither am I.

128
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:52,200
You listen to your husband so blindly.
I regret allowing this marriage.

129
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:55,240
If that's all you have to say,
please excuse me.

130
00:10:57,360 --> 00:11:00,880
If you care about him that much,
think about his social standing.

131
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:06,400
What do you mean by that, Mother?
I don't understand.

132
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:09,160
Your husband and your ex-fiancé
living under the same roof?

133
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:10,800
It'll become a massive scandal.

134
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:11,800
Mother!

135
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:13,240
Don't raise your voice at me.

136
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:16,840
I'm speaking as someone
who is older and wiser. Care to argue?

137
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,240
I won't argue.

138
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:21,440
But my intentions are pure.

139
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:23,920
If Bundit didn't trust Tri,

140
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,360
he wouldn't have invited him here.

141
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:30,600
Besides, unless an insider leaks it,
how would outsiders ever know?

142
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:33,000
How dare you talk back to me like this?

143
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:35,440
Have you become completely rebellious now?

144
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:37,440
I apologize, Mother.

145
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,000
Are you lonely?
Is that why you're fishing here?

146
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:07,760
If I were lonely,

147
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:10,240
I'd go annoy Aunt Gaysorn instead.

148
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:13,520
I don't want to be
a burden to you and Sasi,

149
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,520
so I'm catching my own food.

150
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:19,880
You're overthinking.
She just talks like that.

151
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:21,000
It's nothing.

152
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,640
Not at all.

153
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:26,760
I know your mother-in-law
better than you do.

154
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:33,480
By the way, it's been a month now.

155
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:35,600
Why hasn't she returned to Bangkok yet?

156
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:40,160
She wants to take Sasi back with her,
so she refuses to leave.

157
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,520
Strange.

158
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:47,320
She usually loves her comfort.

159
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:50,280
Why endure this for so long?

160
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:55,240
Merely taking Sasi back to be a librarian

161
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:58,080
doesn't seem that crucial, does it?

162
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:03,920
Stop speculating.

163
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:08,800
What you asked me to help with is done.

164
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:13,280
That fast?

165
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:14,600
Yes.

166
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:16,880
Thank you, District Chief.

167
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:19,200
I'll head back inside.

168
00:13:19,280 --> 00:13:20,480
Yes.

169
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:32,000
<i>I found dirt on Vijarn.</i>
<i>Let's meet up and talk in Phra Nakhon.</i>

170
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:33,560
<i>From Srichan.</i>

171
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:54,160
Any updates?

172
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:57,400
It seems Thatri has run back to Bangkok.

173
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:58,880
How do you know that?

174
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:02,080
My men saw him catch the last boat.

175
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,320
That's perfect.

176
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:07,120
I didn't hold that much of a grudge
against him anyway.

177
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:11,560
I just didn't want him blocking my path.
No need to kill him.

178
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:15,760
Besides, I have an appointment
with an important business partner

179
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:18,040
who's coming down to Phuket.

180
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:21,680
An important partner? Who is it?

181
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:24,760
Have you never wondered

182
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:28,600
where I used to get the smuggled goods
to undercut Ms. Fuangfah?

183
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:33,000
-That means…
-This exact partner

184
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:35,120
was the one supplying me.

185
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:47,720
PHRA NAKHON

186
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:52,560
It has been a long time
since we last met, Mr. Thatri.

187
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,840
Good to see you.

188
00:14:57,240 --> 00:15:00,120
If this were the past,
you'd never get to set foot in here.

189
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:04,280
Even now, I'm still terrified of your men.

190
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:05,840
The past is burned into my mind.

191
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:08,360
You mean the way you beat them all up?

192
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:15,800
But right now, there's something else
that will shock you even more.

193
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:22,640
It's been a few months.
You're already pregnant?

194
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,160
-Well.
-Huh?

195
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:27,960
-Since we reconciled, he's insatiable.
-What?

196
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:31,880
He drags me to bed the second he's free.
How could I not get pregnant?

197
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:35,920
See that? She called me old,
but I've still got plenty of fire…

198
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:40,840
Look at you, so full of pride.

199
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:44,880
Let's go inside.
The sun is scorching. I might faint.

200
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:47,520
Right, let's go.

201
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,200
Watch your step. Careful now.

202
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:57,160
Poj has extensive connections.
We managed to dig up the information fast.

203
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,720
What did you find out?

204
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:03,240
Mr. Vijarn is just a second-class lawyer.

205
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:04,800
He's a high school graduate

206
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:08,080
who passed the exam to practice law
strictly within Phuket.

207
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:10,240
But his legal career

208
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:13,200
helped him build connections,
which led him into business.

209
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:17,640
Do you mean the business
of the Som Song Saeng House?

210
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:20,760
No. An illegal business.

211
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:24,600
There are even rumors

212
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:28,200
that he's in contact
with an old enemy of yours.

213
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:30,280
Who is it?

214
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:33,680
PHUKET

215
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:39,800
The food in Phuket tastes wonderful.

216
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:42,080
If you like it,
you should visit more often.

217
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:45,360
I'd love to,

218
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:47,720
but traveling frequently is difficult now.

219
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:50,400
Since World War ended,

220
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:53,960
the currency has depreciated,
and commodity prices have skyrocketed.

221
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:57,520
Isn't that a good thing?

222
00:16:57,600 --> 00:17:00,600
We can make higher profits
from smuggled goods

223
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:02,320
at inflated prices.

224
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:04,720
But we're running out of supply.

225
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:08,599
High profit means nothing
if there's no merchandise to sell.

226
00:17:11,839 --> 00:17:13,119
What should we do then?

227
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:17,599
Relying on our usual business
won't cut it anymore.

228
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:19,720
We need an alternative solution.

229
00:17:21,599 --> 00:17:24,599
An alternative solution? What is it?

230
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:31,440
No wonder I've been looking
for the source for so long,

231
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:34,720
trying to find out
who was undercutting Fuang.

232
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:39,280
Exactly. And those goods
were stolen from ordinary people.

233
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:41,440
Rice from the rationing system

234
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:43,960
and other supplies
meant for public distribution,

235
00:17:44,040 --> 00:17:45,160
they embezzled all of it.

236
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:51,120
Embezzling rations? How wicked.

237
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:54,040
If I ever see them,
I will knock them flat on the ground.

238
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:55,360
Don't be so fierce, honey.

239
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:57,080
-Ugh.
-Calm down, please.

240
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:59,280
Hearing about them just boils my blood.

241
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:01,520
Calm down, honey.

242
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:03,840
So that's why their merchandise
was priced so cheaply.

243
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:08,240
Even if you hijacked a shipment,
it wouldn't be this cheap.

244
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:13,600
Why is Rajit constantly surrounded
by such terrible people?

245
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:17,240
Exactly. The more I listen, the more I…

246
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:19,720
Woah.

247
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,560
Oh, wait. Chomphu!

248
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:26,800
Chomphu, hurry! Bring her item right now.

249
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:28,400
Is she having morning sickness?

250
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:30,680
Chomphu! Where is it? Hurry up!

251
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:33,880
Coming! It's here, it's here!

252
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:44,720
Works like magic.

253
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:47,440
Morning sickness cured by money?

254
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:49,520
Is there such a thing?

255
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:50,600
That's just how it is.

256
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:54,480
Well, his father's genes
are just too strong.

257
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:56,760
This baby loves money inside the womb.

258
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:59,320
I need to sniff lots of cash
to cure my nausea.

259
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,160
Give me another sniff.

260
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:07,360
Impressive, isn't it?

261
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,960
PHUKET

262
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:24,120
Who is it?

263
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:45,480
A thief?

264
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:06,800
Go mop over there, will you?

265
00:20:10,840 --> 00:20:12,800
Nid. There are thieves in the house.

266
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:14,520
What should we do?

267
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:15,760
I don't know

268
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:16,800
Hit them.

269
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:17,840
-With this?
-Yes.

270
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:19,720
No way.

271
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:23,040
Just walk up and hit him. Okay? Go.

272
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:24,400
Let's go.

273
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:26,440
Come on.

274
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,040
Don't!

275
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:09,160
No…

276
00:21:09,800 --> 00:21:10,960
Don't…

277
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:12,400
Don't!

278
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:15,000
Get out!

279
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:29,200
-Aunt Paetai!
-Don't!

280
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:35,440
Mr. Vijarn!

281
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:48,960
Come here.

282
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:58,360
Die!

283
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:09,240
-Come on.
-Go.

284
00:22:13,240 --> 00:22:14,680
Mr. Vijarn!

285
00:22:14,760 --> 00:22:16,160
-Check on him.
-Mr. Vijarn!

286
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:17,400
Mr. Vijarn!

287
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:21,040
Mr. Vijarn.

288
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:23,480
Mr. Vijarn.

289
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:25,240
Mr. Vijarn.

290
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:27,440
Mr. Vijarn.

291
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:30,680
Nid, go get a doctor right now.

292
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:32,480
Yes.

293
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:35,640
Mr. Vijarn.

294
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:38,800
Mr. Vijarn.

295
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:40,760
Mr. Vijarn. Hang in there.

296
00:22:40,840 --> 00:22:42,320
I've sent Nid to fetch a doctor.

297
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:44,560
Mr. Vijarn.

298
00:22:48,080 --> 00:22:51,040
Mr. Vijarn.

299
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:58,360
I'm so sorry, Auntie.

300
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:00,440
Thank goodness I held back in time.

301
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:01,560
Right.

302
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:05,360
If you hadn't stopped,
I'd probably be dead by now.

303
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:11,520
Now that the thieves broke in,

304
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,800
I can't help but feel terrified.

305
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:15,560
In a house without any men,

306
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:18,320
we can't do much on our own.

307
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:21,240
We were incredibly lucky

308
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:23,280
that Vijarn arrived
just in time to save us.

309
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:24,600
Exactly.

310
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:27,400
Otherwise, we would all be dead
in our own home.

311
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,880
Stop talking nonsense.

312
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:31,440
But it's the truth.
Now that Mr. Thatri is gone,

313
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:35,320
I'm the only man left.
And I don't even know how to fight.

314
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:38,560
If Mr. Vijarn hadn't shown up,

315
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:40,320
what would have happened to us?

316
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:45,440
A house without a man as its pillar

317
00:23:45,520 --> 00:23:47,560
makes criminals bold.

318
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:59,920
Doctor, how is he doing?

319
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:02,320
The stab wound is very deep.

320
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:04,320
Fortunately, it missed any vital organs.

321
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:08,120
Keep him still
and avoid too much movement,

322
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:09,880
or the wound will take longer to heal.

323
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:12,120
Thank you.

324
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,880
Thank you, Doctor.

325
00:24:15,040 --> 00:24:17,840
Jiam, please see the doctor out.

326
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:19,520
Yes, miss.

327
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:21,080
This way, Doctor.

328
00:24:25,120 --> 00:24:27,000
Rajit, go inside and see him.

329
00:24:27,720 --> 00:24:28,840
Yes.

330
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:43,360
Mr. Vijarn.

331
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:45,840
How are you feeling?

332
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:48,360
It's nowhere near my heart.

333
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:53,520
Hey, why are you moving?

334
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:56,320
The doctor just said not to move.

335
00:24:57,120 --> 00:24:58,960
Rajit, go give him a hand.

336
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:00,960
-Yes.
-I can manage.

337
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:02,840
Let me help you.

338
00:25:03,720 --> 00:25:05,000
Easy now.

339
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:10,080
Take it easy.

340
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:14,320
Ms. Paetai.

341
00:25:15,320 --> 00:25:17,000
May I return to rest at my own home?

342
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:20,440
I'm a man,

343
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:24,400
and I have no relations to this family.

344
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:27,080
Staying overnight here

345
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:29,680
wouldn't be proper.

346
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:32,360
Nonsense about what's proper.
You just saved our lives

347
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:34,760
Otherwise, we would all be dead by now.

348
00:25:34,840 --> 00:25:37,360
But I'm still an outsider.

349
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:41,040
To be precise…

350
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:45,160
I'm just an employee. Getting too close

351
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:47,600
might ruin your reputation.

352
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:49,800
Not at all.

353
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:52,360
I've never thought of you that way.

354
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:57,040
You don't despise me then?

355
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:02,080
Miss Rajit.

356
00:26:04,120 --> 00:26:05,880
Will you marry me?

357
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:14,320
Well…

358
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:18,760
Please give me a chance
to take care of you.

359
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:33,760
Vijarn did just risk his life to save us.

360
00:26:33,840 --> 00:26:38,600
And it really would be reassuring
to have a man in this house.

361
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:43,280
But it's entirely up to you.

362
00:26:48,840 --> 00:26:50,680
I think it's just too soon.

363
00:26:56,800 --> 00:26:59,600
I understand. I can wait.

364
00:27:06,920 --> 00:27:10,320
Ms. Paetai, would you mind
having Nid help me home?

365
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:12,960
Sure.

366
00:27:13,040 --> 00:27:15,160
Nid, take him back home.

367
00:27:15,920 --> 00:27:17,120
Yes.

368
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:20,520
Come here. I'll help.

369
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:25,840
Thank you.

370
00:28:09,480 --> 00:28:11,720
My men told me they injured you.

371
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:13,200
Are you all right?

372
00:28:15,920 --> 00:28:17,520
Tell your men

373
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:19,760
if they screw up again, they're dead.

374
00:28:19,840 --> 00:28:21,200
They nearly killed me.

375
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:27,240
Even after I went through all this pain,

376
00:28:27,320 --> 00:28:30,040
Rajit still hasn't agreed to marry me.

377
00:28:30,120 --> 00:28:33,920
So this whole sacrifice
was completely in vain?

378
00:28:36,480 --> 00:28:37,520
Not yet.

379
00:28:39,800 --> 00:28:42,360
She has no one left anyway.

380
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:45,720
Thatri is exposed as a fraud,

381
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:47,920
and Fuangfah is dead.

382
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:51,800
Even Paetai, who always opposed me,

383
00:28:52,320 --> 00:28:53,720
has softened up

384
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:55,520
after encountering those fake thieves.

385
00:28:57,720 --> 00:29:02,560
I'll move into that house
as Rajit's husband.

386
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:05,040
It's only a matter of time.

387
00:29:07,800 --> 00:29:09,160
If you actually move in,

388
00:29:09,800 --> 00:29:11,720
won't it disrupt our operations?

389
00:29:13,520 --> 00:29:15,600
That's not a problem.
In fact, it's perfect.

390
00:29:16,520 --> 00:29:18,720
I'll monitor every single move
inside that house.

391
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:33,400
PHRA NAKHON

392
00:29:40,360 --> 00:29:42,880
So relaxing…

393
00:29:43,840 --> 00:29:45,200
Oh, you're all packed?

394
00:29:45,720 --> 00:29:47,560
I've told the driver to get the car ready.

395
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:49,520
Thank you.

396
00:29:52,960 --> 00:29:53,800
Tri,

397
00:29:53,880 --> 00:29:56,560
now that the secret is out,

398
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:59,000
don't you think it's time
to tell her the truth?

399
00:29:59,080 --> 00:30:01,880
Tell her the truth about what?

400
00:30:01,960 --> 00:30:04,480
You are so stubborn.

401
00:30:07,840 --> 00:30:10,960
I just caused so much trouble.
She probably doesn't want to look at me

402
00:30:12,640 --> 00:30:16,640
She might act like that,
but deep down, she might be thrilled

403
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:18,640
to know you're not her real uncle.

404
00:30:19,440 --> 00:30:21,600
It's up to you to take the first move.

405
00:30:24,040 --> 00:30:25,720
Honestly, I really like that girl.

406
00:30:25,800 --> 00:30:29,160
She's capable, smart, respectful,

407
00:30:29,240 --> 00:30:30,600
and hard-working.

408
00:30:30,680 --> 00:30:33,200
Women like her
are hard to find these days.

409
00:30:34,360 --> 00:30:37,880
Let me know when you need a family elder.
I'll lead the marriage proposal for you.

410
00:30:40,760 --> 00:30:43,960
Please don't. I'm poor.

411
00:30:44,040 --> 00:30:45,440
No woman would ever choose me.

412
00:30:46,040 --> 00:30:48,240
Sri, you saw yourself
why Sasi abandoned me.

413
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:50,960
Oh, come on, Tri.

414
00:30:51,040 --> 00:30:53,120
Rajit and Sasithon are different people.

415
00:30:53,200 --> 00:30:54,880
Don't compare them.

416
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:58,080
I completely agree, sweetheart.

417
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:01,480
Besides, Rajit is wealthy.

418
00:31:01,560 --> 00:31:03,000
She doesn't care about money.

419
00:31:03,760 --> 00:31:06,320
That makes it even worse.
I have nothing but myself.

420
00:31:06,400 --> 00:31:08,840
How can I compare
to a millionaire like her?

421
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:13,120
Well,

422
00:31:14,320 --> 00:31:16,640
just ask whenever you need my assistance.

423
00:31:17,320 --> 00:31:19,440
Don't worry, Tri.

424
00:31:19,520 --> 00:31:21,840
We've always got your back.

425
00:31:24,680 --> 00:31:25,800
Thank you.

426
00:31:34,120 --> 00:31:35,240
I'll take my leave now.

427
00:31:52,840 --> 00:31:54,880
This time we got so little,
just as you said.

428
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:58,800
Before long, it'll be out of stock,
and our profits will plunge.

429
00:32:01,240 --> 00:32:04,760
I told you, didn't I?
We need to find another way.

430
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:08,880
Then just tell me already.
Stop keeping me in suspense.

431
00:32:10,320 --> 00:32:11,320
Hey.

432
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:28,160
What is this stuff?

433
00:32:28,240 --> 00:32:29,680
Heroin.

434
00:32:46,640 --> 00:32:47,640
I won't deal in drugs.

435
00:32:48,440 --> 00:32:49,560
Why the hell not?

436
00:32:49,640 --> 00:32:51,520
I may be a pirate,

437
00:32:51,600 --> 00:32:53,880
but I'm not wicked enough to deal drugs.

438
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:56,320
Opium has already ruined countries,

439
00:32:56,400 --> 00:32:59,080
and you know this stuff
is far deadlier than opium.

440
00:32:59,160 --> 00:33:00,680
Stop overthinking it.

441
00:33:00,760 --> 00:33:03,280
You're a pirate who kills people
all the time anyway.

442
00:33:03,880 --> 00:33:05,160
How is this any different?

443
00:33:05,240 --> 00:33:06,760
Don't play the saint with me.

444
00:33:07,880 --> 00:33:09,560
I only kill those who resist.

445
00:33:09,640 --> 00:33:13,480
But this poison
slaughters everyone blindly.

446
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:17,080
There is nothing more evil than this.

447
00:33:17,920 --> 00:33:21,040
Is that so? But if I don't do this,

448
00:33:21,120 --> 00:33:24,200
I won't have any money,
and neither will you.

449
00:33:24,880 --> 00:33:28,200
I can stage more robberies for cash.
Just leave the drugs out of it.

450
00:33:30,400 --> 00:33:32,240
Are you robbing for the rest of your life?

451
00:33:33,160 --> 00:33:35,680
Trust me. Sell this,

452
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:37,200
and you'll be filthy rich.

453
00:33:37,280 --> 00:33:40,720
You can quit being a pirate
and stop risking your life.

454
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:43,440
You'll be set for life. Isn't that better?

455
00:34:02,200 --> 00:34:03,960
If I decide to sell it,

456
00:34:05,680 --> 00:34:07,240
nothing will stop me.

457
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:16,199
DISTRICT CHIEF'S RESIDENCE

458
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:17,120
Come on in.

459
00:34:23,280 --> 00:34:24,320
Mother.

460
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:30,960
I thought you weren't going to greet me.

461
00:34:31,560 --> 00:34:32,600
Of course I would.

462
00:34:32,679 --> 00:34:35,320
I will always respect you.

463
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:36,880
Thank you.

464
00:34:37,440 --> 00:34:39,800
But really, when you left this house,

465
00:34:39,880 --> 00:34:43,719
I thought I'd never see your face again.

466
00:34:44,920 --> 00:34:46,360
I was away on business,

467
00:34:47,040 --> 00:34:49,120
but I'd always return to see you.

468
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:52,000
After all, I care about you deeply.

469
00:34:53,199 --> 00:34:54,639
Save your breath.

470
00:34:59,240 --> 00:35:02,160
Tri, give my mother a break.

471
00:35:02,240 --> 00:35:03,200
Exactly.

472
00:35:03,720 --> 00:35:07,160
Otherwise, things will just
get awkward under this roof.

473
00:35:08,760 --> 00:35:10,640
Well, she's the one who ruined everything.

474
00:35:10,720 --> 00:35:13,080
If she hadn't spilled
the secret to Vijarn that day…

475
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:16,400
I'm the lawyer for Mr. Thatri's family.

476
00:35:16,480 --> 00:35:17,600
Lawyer?

477
00:35:18,600 --> 00:35:21,600
He's broke. How can he even afford one?

478
00:35:22,840 --> 00:35:23,960
Broke?

479
00:35:24,040 --> 00:35:26,760
<i>He used to be filthy rich,</i>
<i>wealthy beyond belief.</i>

480
00:35:26,840 --> 00:35:29,720
<i>Everyone in Bangkok knows Thatri.</i>

481
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:32,120
…this mess wouldn't have blown up,

482
00:35:32,200 --> 00:35:35,200
and I'd still be
at Som Song Saeng House with…

483
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:41,720
Speaking of Som Song Saeng House…

484
00:35:48,920 --> 00:35:50,560
Is something wrong?

485
00:35:55,720 --> 00:35:56,760
Tri.

486
00:35:57,480 --> 00:35:59,120
I have something to tell you.

487
00:36:09,160 --> 00:36:12,560
How can he suddenly ask for an engagement?
Don't you dare give in, Rajit.

488
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:14,760
Of course I won't.

489
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:20,400
But I'm being pressured every single day.

490
00:36:21,240 --> 00:36:24,680
Just ignore him.
How long can that pressure even last?

491
00:36:25,520 --> 00:36:29,000
Mr. Vijarn got hurt
saving everyone in our house.

492
00:36:29,080 --> 00:36:31,400
How can I just feel absolutely nothing?

493
00:36:32,360 --> 00:36:33,720
He's just putting on an act.

494
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:35,080
How could you fall for his trap?

495
00:36:35,760 --> 00:36:39,000
Uncle Ree, I didn't fall for anything.

496
00:36:39,680 --> 00:36:41,360
It's just that I have no other choice.

497
00:36:44,080 --> 00:36:46,680
No matter what,
don't agree to get engaged.

498
00:36:46,760 --> 00:36:49,000
As a woman, you have everything to lose.

499
00:36:49,080 --> 00:36:50,720
Are you only just realizing this now?

500
00:36:50,800 --> 00:36:54,480
When you asked me to get close
to Mr. Vijarn to spy on him,

501
00:36:54,560 --> 00:36:56,320
you didn't seem to care about that at all.

502
00:36:56,920 --> 00:36:59,400
I didn't expect him
to force your hand like this.

503
00:37:01,240 --> 00:37:04,280
If I knew, I'd never have allowed it.
I care too much about you.

504
00:37:15,040 --> 00:37:18,080
Concerned. I meant
that I'm concerned about you.

505
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:23,520
Let's get back to the engagement.

506
00:37:24,040 --> 00:37:25,880
How exactly is he pressuring you?

507
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:30,280
Every way possible.
Directly and indirectly,

508
00:37:30,360 --> 00:37:32,400
even getting Auntie Paetai to persuade me.

509
00:37:32,480 --> 00:37:35,880
I tried to stall, telling him
we should get to know each other first,

510
00:37:35,960 --> 00:37:37,920
but he refused.

511
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:42,960
He's forcing it that quickly?

512
00:37:43,040 --> 00:37:44,320
Yes.

513
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:47,760
He's planning to invite influential
figures from the entire province.

514
00:37:47,840 --> 00:37:51,960
He wants to force my hand,
so I won't stand a chance of refusing.

515
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:55,400
For just an engagement,

516
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:58,640
why invite so many people?

517
00:38:01,040 --> 00:38:02,040
That's suspicious.

518
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:09,840
PHUKET HOTEL

519
00:38:09,920 --> 00:38:13,280
I've invited influential figures
for the event. The coast is clear.

520
00:38:13,360 --> 00:38:15,040
Prepare to bring the goods in.

521
00:38:16,240 --> 00:38:17,400
Brilliant.

522
00:38:17,480 --> 00:38:22,160
Using your own engagement
as a distraction for the authorities.

523
00:38:23,800 --> 00:38:26,560
If you want to play a big game,
you must be bold.

524
00:38:28,720 --> 00:38:30,680
I really like the way you think.

525
00:38:33,240 --> 00:38:35,360
Leave the rest to me.

526
00:38:35,440 --> 00:38:39,200
Don't worry, everything
will go flawlessly.

527
00:38:39,720 --> 00:38:41,120
I trust you completely.

528
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:14,520
This is the list of goods
ordered by Mr. Vijarn.

529
00:39:19,920 --> 00:39:22,480
Why did he order
so many unnecessary items?

530
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:25,960
He mentioned that
if we order these items now,

531
00:39:26,040 --> 00:39:27,600
we can get them at a lower price.

532
00:39:32,720 --> 00:39:35,120
I just hope they bring
some profit to the company.

533
00:39:48,760 --> 00:39:51,240
He's definitely up to something.

534
00:39:51,320 --> 00:39:52,840
Why invite so many people

535
00:39:53,800 --> 00:39:55,720
just for an engagement?

536
00:39:58,080 --> 00:40:01,200
But Miss Rajit is the granddaughter
of a well-known figure in Phuket.

537
00:40:02,520 --> 00:40:03,920
It doesn't seem that unusual.

538
00:40:05,960 --> 00:40:07,560
I'm not overthinking this.

539
00:40:07,640 --> 00:40:09,600
You seem incredibly intense about this.

540
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:11,880
Is there something more?

541
00:40:15,440 --> 00:40:17,560
I just want to expose Mr. Vijarn.

542
00:40:20,240 --> 00:40:21,640
It's far too suspicious.

543
00:40:22,600 --> 00:40:25,120
The engagement is incredibly rushed,

544
00:40:25,640 --> 00:40:27,560
and Rajit said Mr. Vijarn ordered

545
00:40:27,640 --> 00:40:30,400
a massive shipment of goods
to the company.

546
00:40:31,920 --> 00:40:34,320
There might be illicit items smuggled.

547
00:40:37,040 --> 00:40:38,920
Bringing in those influential figures

548
00:40:40,640 --> 00:40:43,600
is just a way to clear a path
for whatever they are executing.

549
00:41:04,560 --> 00:41:07,400
<i>No matter what,</i>
<i>don't agree to get engaged.</i>

550
00:41:07,480 --> 00:41:09,520
<i>As a woman, you have everything to lose.</i>

551
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:11,920
Are you only just realizing this now?

552
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:15,680
When you asked me to get close
to Mr. Vijarn to spy on him,

553
00:41:15,760 --> 00:41:17,520
you didn't seem to care about that at all.

554
00:41:18,120 --> 00:41:20,240
I didn't expect him
to force your hand like this.

555
00:41:21,920 --> 00:41:25,080
If I knew, I'd never have allowed it.
I care too much about you.

556
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:36,240
He claims he cares,
but he never makes a move.

557
00:41:37,520 --> 00:41:39,720
After all, we aren't even related anymore.

558
00:41:45,560 --> 00:41:47,560
Miss Rajit!

559
00:41:53,480 --> 00:41:54,400
What's wrong, Nid?

560
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:56,960
Miss Rajit, Don Jose is sick.

561
00:41:57,040 --> 00:41:59,120
Huh? How did he get sick?

562
00:41:59,200 --> 00:42:01,680
I have no idea.
He's refusing to eat anything.

563
00:42:11,280 --> 00:42:14,800
DOCTOR SOMSAK

564
00:42:14,880 --> 00:42:16,160
Rajit.

565
00:42:16,240 --> 00:42:17,440
Uncle Ree.

566
00:42:17,520 --> 00:42:20,880
What's wrong with Don Jose?
Nid said he refused to eat anything.

567
00:42:21,480 --> 00:42:23,160
I have no idea.

568
00:42:33,240 --> 00:42:35,320
Doctor, how is Don Jose doing?

569
00:42:36,560 --> 00:42:39,800
I treat humans, not animals.
I have absolutely no idea.

570
00:42:48,240 --> 00:42:51,000
Doctor, can I have some of that bread?

571
00:43:00,480 --> 00:43:01,520
Suddenly he has an appetite.

572
00:43:01,600 --> 00:43:03,000
Maybe he's tired of his food.

573
00:43:03,520 --> 00:43:05,120
Nid kept feeding him chicken breast.

574
00:43:06,720 --> 00:43:10,960
I guess I'll have to take charge
of Don Jose's meals myself.

575
00:43:12,600 --> 00:43:16,080
Or maybe he refused to eat
because he's heartbroken

576
00:43:16,600 --> 00:43:18,400
that the two of you are living apart?

577
00:43:36,880 --> 00:43:37,720
I'll leave you two to it.

578
00:43:47,520 --> 00:43:50,760
If everything is sorted out,
I'll head back now.

579
00:43:53,920 --> 00:43:56,320
I will take Don Jose back home right away.

580
00:44:00,440 --> 00:44:01,600
Let's go, Don Jose.

581
00:44:09,160 --> 00:44:10,880
Oh, it's suddenly pouring?

582
00:44:11,400 --> 00:44:14,120
Let's just wait here
until the rain lets up.

583
00:44:34,080 --> 00:44:36,720
The rain is pouring down.
There's no sign of it letting up.

584
00:44:38,080 --> 00:44:38,960
That's actually good.

585
00:44:41,040 --> 00:44:43,360
Good? How is that a good thing?

586
00:44:46,720 --> 00:44:47,720
Well,

587
00:44:49,040 --> 00:44:50,960
I get to stay with Don Jose a bit longer.

588
00:44:54,480 --> 00:44:56,080
So you only want to be with Don Jose?

589
00:44:58,320 --> 00:45:00,040
I'd love to stay here until tomorrow.

590
00:45:04,320 --> 00:45:08,200
In that case, you can just
stay here with Don Jose.

591
00:45:08,280 --> 00:45:10,280
I'm heading back home.

592
00:45:12,960 --> 00:45:14,320
Wait.

593
00:45:25,440 --> 00:45:26,840
I want to stay with you too.

594
00:45:51,600 --> 00:45:52,600
Then…

595
00:45:55,800 --> 00:45:58,480
I suppose I can stay
to keep Don Jose company too.

596
00:45:59,120 --> 00:46:01,520
I want to be with him
for a long time as well.

597
00:46:32,200 --> 00:46:33,560
-Ahh!
-What?

598
00:46:33,640 --> 00:46:35,760
A lizard! There's a lizard!

599
00:46:36,560 --> 00:46:39,840
-Where?
-Right there!

600
00:46:41,200 --> 00:46:42,120
I can't even see it.

601
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:44,560
Uncle Ree, please chase it away!

602
00:46:44,640 --> 00:46:47,720
Is it gone yet? Uncle Ree.

603
00:46:49,080 --> 00:46:50,560
No, not yet.

604
00:46:50,640 --> 00:46:53,680
-Please scare it away. I'm terrified.
-Alright.

605
00:46:56,280 --> 00:46:57,400
It's gone now.

606
00:48:04,680 --> 00:48:07,240
Put those down for now.
Go grab the ones on the boat.

607
00:48:13,120 --> 00:48:14,280
Be careful with that.

608
00:48:16,600 --> 00:48:17,680
Mr. Vijarn?

609
00:48:39,040 --> 00:48:41,120
Zhang Gong Cheng
is working for Mr. Vijarn?

610
00:48:41,200 --> 00:48:43,400
Yes, I saw it with my own eyes.

611
00:48:43,480 --> 00:48:44,840
They were definitely together.

612
00:48:46,800 --> 00:48:48,840
I never expected this from Mr. Vijarn.

613
00:48:49,440 --> 00:48:51,080
He stayed at the house for so long,

614
00:48:51,160 --> 00:48:55,040
acting quiet and harmless,
but he's actually evil to the core.

615
00:48:55,120 --> 00:48:58,240
Fuang also seemed harmless at first,
and look how evil she turned out.

616
00:49:02,120 --> 00:49:03,920
Was there anything suspicious

617
00:49:04,000 --> 00:49:05,840
about the cargo he was moving?

618
00:49:06,560 --> 00:49:08,640
Too bad I couldn't see what was inside.

619
00:49:08,720 --> 00:49:11,400
But you know where they're planning
to store those goods?

620
00:49:11,480 --> 00:49:12,640
I do.

621
00:49:13,240 --> 00:49:16,000
Good. Now all that's left
is to go check out that cargo.

622
00:49:56,000 --> 00:49:57,040
Rajit.

623
00:49:58,240 --> 00:49:59,600
You scared me.

624
00:49:59,680 --> 00:50:01,800
Walking in so quietly like that.

625
00:50:02,400 --> 00:50:04,920
I saw you sitting here looking stressed,
drawing a frowning face.

626
00:50:12,320 --> 00:50:14,880
Why did you grab my stick?

627
00:50:49,360 --> 00:50:50,880
Are you stressed about the engagement?

628
00:50:53,200 --> 00:50:54,920
Well, shouldn't I be?

629
00:50:59,920 --> 00:51:01,680
Hang in there, Rajit.

630
00:51:03,680 --> 00:51:07,960
I'm certain there's something hidden
inside the goods Mr. Vijarn ordered.

631
00:51:09,880 --> 00:51:11,720
It might be illegal contraband.

632
00:51:12,840 --> 00:51:16,640
Once we get our hands on it,
we can put him behind bars,

633
00:51:17,520 --> 00:51:19,040
and you won't have to marry him.

634
00:51:22,040 --> 00:51:26,440
An engagement should only happen
with someone you love.

635
00:51:31,440 --> 00:51:33,720
I won't let you marry
a man you don't love.

636
00:51:36,800 --> 00:51:38,640
We barely have any time left.

637
00:51:39,160 --> 00:51:40,720
Will we make it in time?

638
00:51:42,840 --> 00:51:43,680
We will.

639
00:51:44,840 --> 00:51:46,280
It all ends tonight.

640
00:52:11,880 --> 00:52:14,000
Freeze! Don't move!

641
00:52:14,520 --> 00:52:15,840
Drop your weapons

642
00:52:15,920 --> 00:52:17,320
and put your hands up!

643
00:52:29,760 --> 00:52:30,800
Get down!

644
00:52:31,920 --> 00:52:33,000
Stay down!

645
00:52:33,760 --> 00:52:36,480
Search the entire place.
Check for any illicit items.

646
00:52:36,560 --> 00:52:37,680
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

647
00:52:48,760 --> 00:52:50,840
The District Chief searched our warehouse?

648
00:52:52,360 --> 00:52:53,680
Then what about our goods?

649
00:53:21,080 --> 00:53:22,320
We found nothing, sir.

650
00:53:22,400 --> 00:53:23,680
It's just coffee beans.

651
00:53:49,080 --> 00:53:50,440
We've been tricked.

652
00:53:58,040 --> 00:54:01,560
I'm sorry, District Chief.
I underestimated them.

653
00:54:18,240 --> 00:54:20,360
Those fools.

654
00:54:20,440 --> 00:54:23,560
No matter how hard they search,
they'll never find our goods.

655
00:54:23,640 --> 00:54:24,640
Right, Mr. Sathit?

656
00:54:35,200 --> 00:54:36,240
The raid failed?

657
00:54:37,080 --> 00:54:38,240
We were completely fooled.

658
00:54:39,480 --> 00:54:41,920
What should we do next, Uncle Ree?

659
00:54:43,280 --> 00:54:45,640
This failure will cost
the District Chief dearly.

660
00:54:45,720 --> 00:54:47,920
Calling in backup only to find nothing.

661
00:54:48,640 --> 00:54:52,160
Mr. Vijarn is clever.
He did this to ruin my credibility,

662
00:54:52,240 --> 00:54:53,920
so that no one will believe me again.

663
00:54:54,960 --> 00:54:58,760
Do you think they will still try
to smuggle the goods into Phuket?

664
00:54:59,520 --> 00:55:00,560
Definitely.

665
00:55:00,640 --> 00:55:03,600
And if I had to guess, they'll smuggle it
on your engagement day.

666
00:55:03,680 --> 00:55:06,440
All the influential figures
in the province will be there,

667
00:55:06,520 --> 00:55:08,960
and police will be distracted.

668
00:55:09,040 --> 00:55:11,120
It's their perfect opportunity
to move the cargo.

669
00:55:11,720 --> 00:55:14,520
So that means Mr. Vijarn
is going to use the engagement

670
00:55:14,600 --> 00:55:17,400
as a cover to smuggle illegal contraband?

671
00:55:19,040 --> 00:55:19,920
Yes.

672
00:55:25,800 --> 00:55:27,480
In that case, I'm getting engaged.

673
00:55:28,520 --> 00:55:30,400
Rajit, don't do this. I won't allow it.

674
00:55:32,720 --> 00:55:33,960
Miss Rajit,

675
00:55:34,040 --> 00:55:36,200
have you really agreed
to accept my proposal?

676
00:55:36,920 --> 00:55:39,200
Yes. You have no flaws,

677
00:55:39,280 --> 00:55:41,200
and you've helped us so much.

678
00:55:41,720 --> 00:55:43,880
How could I possibly refuse you?

679
00:55:45,760 --> 00:55:48,800
Well, well. And you kept
playing hard to get for so long.

680
00:55:51,240 --> 00:55:54,400
I'll handle all the arrangements myself.

681
00:55:55,120 --> 00:55:56,240
Thank you, Aunt Pae.

682
00:55:57,440 --> 00:56:00,480
But there's no need
for a massive celebration.

683
00:56:00,560 --> 00:56:02,560
An intimate event
with just family is enough.

684
00:56:03,480 --> 00:56:04,480
I understand.

685
00:56:05,200 --> 00:56:06,960
Absolutely not, Miss Rajit.

686
00:56:07,560 --> 00:56:10,920
You mean the world to me,
and I must honor you properly.

687
00:56:12,440 --> 00:56:14,040
As I mentioned before,

688
00:56:14,120 --> 00:56:16,040
this has to be a grand event.

689
00:56:16,120 --> 00:56:19,080
Every influential figure in Phuket
will be at our celebration.

690
00:56:22,080 --> 00:56:25,400
Then, whatever you think is best.

691
00:56:26,160 --> 00:56:28,240
Yes. Thank you.

692
00:56:48,840 --> 00:56:50,120
<i>On my engagement day,</i>

693
00:56:51,040 --> 00:56:54,960
<i>all the police in Phuket will be here</i>
<i>to provide security.</i>

694
00:56:56,360 --> 00:56:58,240
I don't approve of this engagement.

695
00:56:58,760 --> 00:57:01,360
<i>Rajit, I love you.</i>

696
00:57:03,840 --> 00:57:07,560
Is it that dangerous, Uncle Ree?
What you're planning to do today?

697
00:57:07,640 --> 00:57:09,960
<i>Do you really think</i>
<i>Thatri would be stupid enough</i>

698
00:57:10,040 --> 00:57:13,680
to throw his life away here,
just to save a worthless nobody like him?

699
00:57:13,760 --> 00:57:15,320
<i>Thatri will show up.</i>

700
00:57:53,040 --> 00:57:55,400
Subtitle translation by:
Khathathong Thongtumlueng
